  "notes": "West leads the ♥A against 4♠. The defense takes the first 3 heart tricks. South ruffs the next heart lead and has only to dispose of his club loser.\n\nSouth must ruff his club loser in the dummy. After cashing the ♣A, South should be careful to ruff his ♣2 with the ♠A. If the ♣2 is ruffed with the ♠Q, the spade suit is blocked. After cashing the ♠A, North will have only diamonds left. South will go down if diamonds are 4-1 as the defense will be able to ruff the second round.\n\nBy ruffing the ♣2 with the ♠A, South gives himself an easy way back to his hand to draw trump. South can overtake the ♠Q with the ♠K, draw trump, and take the balance.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
